module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.Affine.CartesianColimit
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Thickenings.SquareZeroExtensionChartOpenImmersion

/-!
# The chart diagram of a square-zero extension is cartesian over the reduction

Let `0 ⟶ ℐ ⟶ 𝒜 ⟶ 𝒪_X ⟶ 0` be a square-zero extension of the structure sheaf of an algebraic
space `X` over `Y`, in the sense of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension`, and let
`h : U ⟶ V` be a morphism of the small étale site of `X` between objects with affine underlying
scheme.  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.reductionChartSpec` is the natural
transformation `Spec(𝒪_X(U)) ⟶ Spec(𝒜(U))` of chart diagrams induced by the reduction.  This
file proves that **its naturality square at `h` is cartesian**:
`Spec(𝒪_X(U)) = Spec(𝒜(U)) ×_{Spec(𝒜(V))} Spec(𝒪_X(V))`.

This is the compatibility a gluing datum owes — the analogue, for the chart diagram of
[Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT], of the field `isPullback_res` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.BasisGluingData`.  It says that the chart `U` of `X` is cut out of the
chart `Spec(𝒜(U))` of the extension by the *same* equations that cut `V` out of `Spec(𝒜(V))`, so
that the first-order thickenings
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isFirstOrderThickening_chartThickening_of_isAffine`
of the individual charts are compatible along the arrows of the diagram.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`: **the kernel
  ideal of the reduction over `U` is exactly the ideal generated by the image of the kernel ideal
  over `V`.**  This is the identity `K_V · 𝒜(U) = K_U` of the proof of the source; the inclusion
  that is not formal is `…ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine`: **the naturality
  square of the reduction on sections is a pushout of rings**, i.e.
  `𝒪_X(U) = 𝒜(U) ⊗_{𝒜(V)} 𝒪_X(V)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPullback_reductionChartSpec_app_of_isAffine`:
  **consequently the naturality square of `reductionChartSpec` at `h` is cartesian.**

## Implementation notes

The ideal identity is the whole content.  Its easy inclusion
`Ideal.map (res 𝒜) K_V ≤ K_U` is the naturality of the reduction on sections
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.π_app_map_apply`) through
`Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap`; the other inclusion is
`…ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`, which comes from the base change
`…isBaseChange_ker_app_of_isAffine` and is where the étaleness of the arrows of the diagram is
used.

From the identity the pushout is
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.CartesianColimit.isPushout_of_surjective_of_ker_eq`, whose
surjectivity hypotheses are the surjectivity of the reduction over the two affine charts, and the
cartesian square is `AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout`.  Note which pair of
parallel edges has to be surjective: it is the two reductions `π_V` and `π_U`, not the two
restriction maps of `𝒜` and of `𝒪_X`, which are localizations and not surjective.  That is why
the square is stated with the reductions as the "vertical" edges of the pushout.

**Why an `Algebra` instance and a compatibility are among the hypotheses.**  The lemma
`…ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine` is stated for an arbitrary `Algebra (𝒜(V)) (𝒜(U))` whose
`algebraMap` is the restriction map, because the base change it is read off from is a statement
about modules.  The conclusions here mention no algebra structure, so the instance is an
argument of the statement only, and `RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra` discharges it at the
restriction map's own `RingHom.toAlgebra`.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.**  This is one compatibility of the diagram whose colimit the proof
of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT] takes; it constructs no ambient algebraic space and identifies no
structure sheaf, and no declaration here quantifies over more than a single pair of charts.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05ZT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01LH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01LH), the gluing over a basis,
  whose datum asks for exactly this cartesian square.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

namespace SquareZeroExtension

variable {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} {f : X ⟶ Y} (E : SquareZeroExtension B S hS f)

/-- **The kernel ideal of the reduction over an affine chart is exactly the ideal generated by
the image of the kernel ideal over an affine chart it maps to.**

This is the identity `K_V · 𝒜(U) = K_U` of the proof of [Stacks Project, Tag 05ZT].  The
inclusion `K_U ≤ K_V · 𝒜(U)` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`; the reverse one
holds over every pair of charts, being the naturality of the reduction on sections. -/
theorem ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom) :
    RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom =
      Ideal.map (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom (RingHom.ker (E.π.hom.app (op V)).hom) := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [← halg]
    exact ker_le_map_ker_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg
  · rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro x hx
    change (E.π.hom.app (op U)).hom ((E.A.obj.map h.op).hom x) = 0
    rw [SquareZeroExtension.π_app_map_apply B S hS E h x, RingHom.mem_ker.mp hx, map_zero]

/-- **The naturality square of the reduction on sections over affine charts is a pushout of
rings**: `𝒪_X(U) = 𝒜(U) ⊗_{𝒜(V)} 𝒪_X(V)`.

The two surjective parallel edges are the reductions `𝒜(V) ⟶ 𝒪_X(V)` and `𝒜(U) ⟶ 𝒪_X(U)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine`), and the kernel
identity is `…ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine`; the square is then
`AlgebraicGeometry.FormalSpace.CartesianColimit.isPushout_of_surjective_of_ker_eq`. -/
theorem isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom) :
    IsPushout (E.π.hom.app (op V)) (E.A.obj.map h.op)
      ((smallEtaleRingedTopos B S hS X).O.obj.map h.op) (E.π.hom.app (op U)) :=
  FormalSpace.CartesianColimit.isPushout_of_surjective_of_ker_eq _ _ _ _
    (E.π.hom.naturality h.op).symm
    (SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E V hV)
    (SquareZeroExtension.surjective_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E U hU)
    (ker_app_eq_map_ker_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg)

/-- **The naturality square of the reduction of the chart diagrams at an arrow between affine
charts is cartesian**:
`Spec(𝒪_X(U)) = Spec(𝒜(U)) ×_{Spec(𝒜(V))} Spec(𝒪_X(V))`.

This is the pullback compatibility a gluing datum owes: the chart `U` sits inside `Spec(𝒜(U))`
as the base change of the way `V` sits inside `Spec(𝒜(V))`.  It is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SquareZeroExtension.isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine` read through
`AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout`. -/
theorem isPullback_reductionChartSpec_app_of_isAffine {U V : SmallEtale B S hS X.1} (h : U ⟶ V)
    (hU : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj U)))
    (hV : IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS X.1).obj V)))
    [Algebra (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U))]
    (halg : algebraMap (E.A.obj.obj (op V)) (E.A.obj.obj (op U)) = (E.A.obj.map h.op).hom) :
    IsPullback ((structureSheafChartSpec B S hS X).map h)
      ((reductionChartSpec B S hS E).app U)
      ((reductionChartSpec B S hS E).app V) ((chartSpec B S hS E).map h) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.isPullback_SpecMap_of_isPushout _ _ _ _
    (isPushout_π_app_of_isAffine B S hS E h hU hV halg)

end SquareZeroExtension

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
